  "$comment": "ERP-neutral functional-entity vocabulary (ADR W7, issue #111). Mappings and DQ rules reference entity_id, never free text — that is what makes two ERPs comparable by construction. Changes are PRs owned by the architecture role; bump `version` on every change. Hard cap: 60 entities. Local additions go in as is_custom entities via loadVocabulary(), never by editing this file ad hoc. D365FO is the pivot structure — every entity carries its D365FO logical (data entities) and physical (tables) reference; source ERPs map onto it via aliases and counterparts.",
